{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KRVjfiAoRosctWmGoHdstM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-82t — Acceptance Criteria: Re-enable Unit Tests in CI Pipeline\n2\t\n3\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-82t  \n4\t**Title:** Re-enable unit tests in CI pipeline (main-ci-deploy.yml)  \n5\t**Type:** Task\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## AC-1: Test Step Enabled\n10\t\n11\t**Given** the `main-ci-deploy.yml` workflow file  \n12\t**When** viewing the file in the repository  \n13\t**Then**:\n14\t- Lines containing \"Run unit tests\" step are **not commented out**\n15\t- Step has `id: tests` identifier\n16\t- Step appears in the CI job steps list\n17\t\n18\t**Verification:**\n19\t```bash\n20\t# Check that test step is uncommented\n21\tgrep -A 7 \"name: Run unit tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml | head -8\n22\t# Should show uncommented YAML (no leading # symbols)\n23\t\n24\t# Verify in GitHub UI\n25\t# Navigate to: .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n26\t# Line ~62-69 should show active step (no comment syntax)\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## AC-2: Correct Test Command\n32\t\n33\t**Given** the test step is enabled  \n34\t**When** examining the step configuration  \n35\t**Then** the `run` command is:\n36\t```yaml\n37\trun: |\n38\t  pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n39\t    -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\t**Verification:**\n43\t```bash\n44\t# Extract pytest command from workflow\n45\tgrep -A 2 \"pytest tests/\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n46\t\n47\t# Expected output:\n48\t#     pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n49\t#       -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t**Breakdown:**\n53\t- ✅ `tests/` — Run tests in tests directory\n54\t- ✅ `-v` — Verbose output\n55\t- ✅ `--tb=short` — Short traceback format\n56\t- ✅ `--maxfail=10` — Stop after 10 failures\n57\t- ✅ `-m \"not integration and not slow\"` — Exclude integration and slow tests\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t\n61\t## AC-3: Database Configuration\n62\t\n63\t**Given** the test step is enabled  \n64\t**When** examining the step's `env` section  \n65\t**Then** `DATABASE_URL` is set to:\n66\t```yaml\n67\tenv:\n68\t  DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t**Verification:**\n72\t```bash\n73\t# Check DATABASE_URL in workflow\n74\tgrep -A 1 \"DATABASE_URL:\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n75\t\n76\t# Expected:\n77\t#     DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t**Component validation:**\n81\t- ✅ Protocol: `postgresql://`\n82\t- ✅ User: `test`\n83\t- ✅ Password: `test`\n84\t- ✅ Host: `localhost` (service container)\n85\t- ✅ Port: `5432` (mapped from service)\n86\t- ✅ Database: `quantagent_test` (matches service config)\n87\t\n88\t---\n89\t\n90\t## AC-4: No Error Tolerance\n91\t\n92\t**Given** the test step configuration  \n93\t**When** examining the step for error handling  \n94\t**Then**:\n95\t- `continue-on-error: true` is **NOT present** in the step\n96\t- No other error suppression directives exist\n97\t\n98\t**Verification:**\n99\t```bash\n100\t# Check that continue-on-error is NOT in test step\n101\tgrep -A 10 \"name: Run unit tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml | \\\n102\t  grep \"continue-on-error\"\n103\t\n104\t# Expected: (no output - grep finds nothing)\n105\t# Exit code: 1 (pattern not found)\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\t**Negative test (anti-pattern detection):**\n109\t```bash\n110\t# Verify test step will fail on error\n111\t# (default GitHub Actions behavior when continue-on-error absent)\n112\tyq eval '.jobs.ci.steps[] | select(.name == \"Run unit tests\") | has(\"continue-on-error\")' \\\n113\t  .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n114\t\n115\t# Expected: false (or key doesn't exist)\n116\t```\n117\t\n118\t---\n119\t\n120\t## AC-5: Deployment Blocking\n121\t\n122\t**Given** tests fail in CI  \n123\t**When** the CI job completes  \n124\t**Then**:\n125\t- CI job status is **failure** (red ❌)\n126\t- `deploy-qa` job does **not** run\n127\t- Telegram notification sent with `failed_step: Unit tests`\n128\t\n129\t**Verification (simulated failure):**\n130\t\n131\t1. **Introduce test failure:**\n132\t   ```bash\n133\t   # Temporarily break a test\n134\t   echo \"def test_fail(): assert False\" >> tests/test_temporary.py\n135\t   git add tests/test_temporary.py\n136\t   git commit -m \"Test: Verify CI blocks on test failure\"\n137\t   git push origin main\n138\t   ```\n139\t\n140\t2. **Observe GitHub Actions:**\n141\t   - CI job shows ❌ red status\n142\t   - \"Run unit tests\" step failed\n143\t   - \"Determine overall status\" step failed with `failed_step=Unit tests`\n144\t   - `deploy-qa` job is **skipped** (not run)\n145\t\n146\t3. **Check Telegram:**\n147\t   - Notification received with:\n148\t     ```\n149\t     🚨 CI Failure\n150\t     Failed step: Unit tests\n151\t     Logs: [link]\n152\t     ```\n153\t\n154\t4. **Cleanup:**\n155\t   ```bash\n156\t   git rm tests/test_temporary.py\n157\t   git commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test failure\"\n158\t   git push origin main\n159\t   ```\n160\t\n161\t---\n162\t\n163\t## AC-6: Success Path Unchanged\n164\t\n165\t**Given** all tests pass in CI  \n166\t**When** the CI job completes  \n167\t**Then**:\n168\t- CI job status is **success** (green ✅)\n169\t- `deploy-qa` job runs (triggered by `needs: ci`)\n170\t- Telegram notifications for both CI success and deploy success\n171\t\n172\t**Verification (normal operation):**\n173\t\n174\t1. **Push valid change:**\n175\t   ```bash\n176\t   # Make trivial documentation change\n177\t   echo \"# Test CI\" >> docs/test_ci.md\n178\t   git add docs/test_ci.md\n179\t   git commit -m \"Test: Verify CI passes and deploys\"\n180\t   git push origin main\n181\t   ```\n182\t\n183\t2. **Observe GitHub Actions:**\n184\t   - CI job shows ✅ green status\n185\t   - All steps passed (lint + tests)\n186\t   - `deploy-qa` job runs after CI completes\n187\t   - QA deployment succeeds\n188\t\n189\t3. **Check Telegram:**\n190\t   - First notification:\n191\t     ```\n192\t     ✅ CI passed\n193\t     Commit: [hash]\n194\t     Message: Test: Verify CI passes and deploys\n195\t     ```\n196\t   - Second notification (after deploy):\n197\t     ```\n198\t     🚀 QA Deploy Success\n199\t     URL: https://qa.fedes.dev\n200\t     ```\n201\t\n202\t4. **Cleanup:**\n203\t   ```bash\n204\t   git rm docs/test_ci.md\n205\t   git commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test file\"\n206\t   git push origin main\n207\t   ```\n208\t\n209\t---\n210\t\n211\t## Edge Cases\n212\t\n213\t### EC-1: Empty Test Suite\n214\t**Given** no tests exist in `tests/` directory  \n215\t**When** CI runs  \n216\t**Then** pytest reports \"no tests collected\" but **exits 0** (success)\n217\t\n218\t**Expected behavior:** CI passes (no tests = no failures)\n219\t\n220\t**Verification:**\n221\t```bash\n222\t# Check pytest behavior with no tests\n223\tpytest --collect-only tests/ | grep \"no tests collected\"\n224\techo $?  # Should be 0 (success)\n225\t```\n226\t\n227\t### EC-2: Database Service Failure\n228\t**Given** PostgreSQL service fails to start  \n229\t**When** test step attempts to run  \n230\t**Then**:\n231\t- Tests fail with connection error\n232\t- CI job fails\n233\t- Deployment blocked\n234\t\n235\t**Expected behavior:** Health checks should prevent this (service has `--health-cmd pg_isready`)\n236\t\n237\t**Monitoring:** Check GitHub Actions logs for PostgreSQL service health\n238\t\n239\t### EC-3: Import Errors\n240\t**Given** tests have import errors (e.g., missing dependency)  \n241\t**When** pytest collects tests  \n242\t**Then**:\n243\t- Pytest reports collection error\n244\t- CI job fails\n245\t- Deployment blocked\n246\t\n247\t**Expected behavior:** Same as test failure (blocks deployment)\n248\t\n249\t### EC-4: Timeout (No Response)\n250\t**Given** a test hangs indefinitely  \n251\t**When** CI runs tests  \n252\t**Then**:\n253\t- GitHub Actions job timeout (default: 360 min, unlikely to hit)\n254\t- Job fails\n255\t- Deployment blocked\n256\t\n257\t**Expected behavior:** `maxfail=10` ensures fail-fast, but no explicit timeout on test step\n258\t\n259\t**Mitigation (if needed):** Add `timeout-minutes: 10` to test step\n260\t\n261\t---\n262\t\n263\t## Performance Criteria\n264\t\n265\t### P-1: CI Duration\n266\t**Given** the full CI pipeline (lint + tests + deploy)  \n267\t**When** all steps run successfully  \n268\t**Then**:\n269\t- CI job completes in < 10 minutes\n270\t- Test step specifically < 5 minutes\n271\t\n272\t**Measurement:**\n273\t- Check GitHub Actions duration in UI\n274\t- Monitor over 10 runs to establish baseline\n275\t\n276\t**Acceptance threshold:**\n277\t- 🟢 < 5 min: Excellent\n278\t- 🟡 5-10 min: Acceptable\n279\t- 🔴 > 10 min: Investigate optimization\n280\t\n281\t### P-2: Resource Usage\n282\t**Given** tests run with PostgreSQL service  \n283\t**When** monitoring GitHub Actions runner  \n284\t**Then**:\n285\t- Memory usage < 2 GB\n286\t- No OOM errors\n287\t\n288\t**Expected:** Standard unit tests should be lightweight\n289\t\n290\t---\n291\t\n292\t## Negative Test Cases\n293\t\n294\t### NT-1: Lint Failure Still Blocks\n295\t**Given** lint fails (ruff check finds errors)  \n296\t**When** CI runs  \n297\t**Then**:\n298\t- CI fails before running tests\n299\t- Tests are **not** run (fail-fast)\n300\t- Deployment blocked\n301\t\n302\t**Verification:**\n303\t```bash\n304\t# Introduce lint error\n305\techo \"import os,sys\" >> quantagent/temporary.py  # Multiple imports on one line\n306\tgit add quantagent/temporary.py\n307\tgit commit -m \"Test: Verify lint failure blocks\"\n308\tgit push origin main\n309\t\n310\t# Expected:\n311\t# - Lint step fails\n312\t# - Test step doesn't run\n313\t# - Deploy blocked\n314\t```\n315\t\n316\t### NT-2: Test Step ID Correct\n317\t**Given** test step is enabled  \n318\t**When** examining step configuration  \n319\t**Then** `id: tests` is present\n320\t\n321\t**Why it matters:** `steps.tests.outcome` is referenced in status determination\n322\t\n323\t**Verification:**\n324\t```bash\n325\tgrep \"id: tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n326\t# Expected: line containing \"id: tests\" (uncommented)\n327\t```\n328\t\n329\t---\n330\t\n331\t## Integration with Existing Workflow\n332\t\n333\t### Telegram Notifications\n334\t**Existing logic should work without modification:**\n335\t\n336\t1. **CI Failure Notification:**\n337\t   ```bash\n338\t   Failed step: ${{ steps.status.outputs.failed_step || 'Unknown' }}\n339\t   ```\n340\t   - If tests fail: `failed_step=Unit tests`\n341\t   - If lint fails: `failed_step=Lint`\n342\t\n343\t2. **CI Success Notification:**\n344\t   - Sent only if all steps pass\n345\t   - Existing logic unchanged\n346\t\n347\t3. **Deploy Notifications:**\n348\t   - Only triggered if `deploy-qa` job runs\n349\t   - Blocked by CI failure\n350\t\n351\t**No changes needed to notification logic** — already handles test failures.\n352\t\n353\t---\n354\t\n355\t## Manual Test Procedure\n356\t\n357\t### Setup\n358\t```bash\n359\t# Clone repo and switch to feature branch\n360\tgit clone <repo>\n361\tcd QuantAgent\n362\tgit checkout feature/QuantAgent-82t-ci-test-enablement\n363\t```\n364\t\n365\t### Test 1: Verify Uncommenting\n366\t```bash\n367\t# Check file diff\n368\tgit diff main .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n369\t\n370\t# Should show:\n371\t# - Removed: # (comment symbols) from lines 62-69\n372\t# - Removed: continue-on-error: true\n373\t# - Changed: maxfail=5 → maxfail=10\n374\t```\n375\t\n376\t### Test 2: Simulate Success\n377\t```bash\n378\t# Push to main (after blockers resolved)\n379\tgit push origin main\n380\t\n381\t# Monitor GitHub Actions:\n382\t# 1. CI job runs\n383\t# 2. Lint passes\n384\t# 3. Tests run and pass\n385\t# 4. Deploy job runs\n386\t# 5. QA deployment succeeds\n387\t\n388\t# Check Telegram:\n389\t# - ✅ CI passed\n390\t# - 🚀 QA Deploy Success\n391\t```\n392\t\n393\t### Test 3: Simulate Failure\n394\t```bash\n395\t# Create failing test\n396\techo \"def test_fail(): assert False\" >> tests/test_ci_verification.py\n397\tgit add tests/test_ci_verification.py\n398\tgit commit -m \"CI Test: Verify failure blocks deployment\"\n399\tgit push origin main\n400\t\n401\t# Monitor GitHub Actions:\n402\t# 1. CI job runs\n403\t# 2. Lint passes\n404\t# 3. Tests run and FAIL\n405\t# 4. Deploy job SKIPPED\n406\t\n407\t# Check Telegram:\n408\t# - 🚨 CI Failure\n409\t# - Failed step: Unit tests\n410\t\n411\t# Cleanup\n412\tgit rm tests/test_ci_verification.py\n413\tgit commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test failure\"\n414\tgit push origin main\n415\t```\n416\t\n417\t---\n418\t\n419\t## Definition of Done (Testing Checklist)\n420\t\n421\t- [ ] AC-1: Test step uncommented in workflow file\n422\t- [ ] AC-2: Correct pytest command (`maxfail=10`, markers)\n423\t- [ ] AC-3: DATABASE_URL configured correctly\n424\t- [ ] AC-4: No `continue-on-error: true` present\n425\t- [ ] AC-5: Test failure blocks deployment (verified)\n426\t- [ ] AC-6: Test success allows deployment (verified)\n427\t- [ ] EC-1: Empty test suite handled gracefully\n428\t- [ ] EC-2: Database service health checks working\n429\t- [ ] P-1: CI completes in < 10 minutes\n430\t- [ ] NT-1: Lint failure still blocks (not bypassed)\n431\t- [ ] NT-2: Test step ID is `tests` (for status check)\n432\t- [ ] Manual Test 2 (success path) completed\n433\t- [ ] Manual Test 3 (failure path) completed\n434\t- [ ] Telegram notifications received for all scenarios\n435\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c01d0b6d-817c-43ca-ba9d-d72fdeeef887","uuid":"60db983d-f580-4bb8-805e-5ddf96d76287","timestamp":"2026-05-04T17:53:50.232Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/QuantAgent/QuantAgent-82t/implementer-20260504T174542Z/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-82t-AC-ci-test-enablement.md","content":"# QuantAgent-82t — Acceptance Criteria: Re-enable Unit Tests in CI Pipeline\n\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-82t  \n**Title:** Re-enable unit tests in CI pipeline (main-ci-deploy.yml)  \n**Type:** Task\n\n---\n\n## AC-1: Test Step Enabled\n\n**Given** the `main-ci-deploy.yml` workflow file  \n**When** viewing the file in the repository  \n**Then**:\n- Lines containing \"Run unit tests\" step are **not commented out**\n- Step has `id: tests` identifier\n- Step appears in the CI job steps list\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Check that test step is uncommented\ngrep -A 7 \"name: Run unit tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml | head -8\n# Should show uncommented YAML (no leading # symbols)\n\n# Verify in GitHub UI\n# Navigate to: .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n# Line ~62-69 should show active step (no comment syntax)\n```\n\n---\n\n## AC-2: Correct Test Command\n\n**Given** the test step is enabled  \n**When** examining the step configuration  \n**Then** the `run` command is:\n```yaml\nrun: |\n  pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n    -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Extract pytest command from workflow\ngrep -A 2 \"pytest tests/\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n\n# Expected output:\n#     pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 \\\n#       -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n```\n\n**Breakdown:**\n- ✅ `tests/` — Run tests in tests directory\n- ✅ `-v` — Verbose output\n- ✅ `--tb=short` — Short traceback format\n- ✅ `--maxfail=10` — Stop after 10 failures\n- ✅ `-m \"not integration and not slow\"` — Exclude integration and slow tests\n\n---\n\n## AC-3: Database Configuration\n\n**Given** the test step is enabled  \n**When** examining the step's `env` section  \n**Then** `DATABASE_URL` is set to:\n```yaml\nenv:\n  DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Check DATABASE_URL in workflow\ngrep -A 1 \"DATABASE_URL:\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n\n# Expected:\n#     DATABASE_URL: postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test\n```\n\n**Component validation:**\n- ✅ Protocol: `postgresql://`\n- ✅ User: `test`\n- ✅ Password: `test`\n- ✅ Host: `localhost` (service container)\n- ✅ Port: `5432` (mapped from service)\n- ✅ Database: `quantagent_test` (matches service config)\n\n---\n\n## AC-4: No Error Tolerance\n\n**Given** the test step configuration  \n**When** examining the step for error handling  \n**Then**:\n- `continue-on-error: true` is **NOT present** in the step\n- No other error suppression directives exist\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Check that continue-on-error is NOT in test step\ngrep -A 10 \"name: Run unit tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml | \\\n  grep \"continue-on-error\"\n\n# Expected: (no output - grep finds nothing)\n# Exit code: 1 (pattern not found)\n```\n\n**Negative test (anti-pattern detection):**\n```bash\n# Verify test step will fail on error\n# (default GitHub Actions behavior when continue-on-error absent)\nyq eval '.jobs.ci.steps[] | select(.name == \"Run unit tests\") | has(\"continue-on-error\")' \\\n  .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n\n# Expected: false (or key doesn't exist)\n```\n\n---\n\n## AC-5: Deployment Blocking\n\n**Given** tests fail in CI  \n**When** the CI job completes  \n**Then**:\n- CI job status is **failure** (red ❌)\n- `deploy-qa` job does **not** run\n- Telegram notification sent with `failed_step: Unit tests`\n\n**Verification (simulated failure):**\n\n1. **Introduce test failure:**\n   ```bash\n   # Temporarily break a test\n   echo \"def test_fail(): assert False\" >> tests/test_temporary.py\n   git add tests/test_temporary.py\n   git commit -m \"Test: Verify CI blocks on test failure\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n2. **Observe GitHub Actions:**\n   - CI job shows ❌ red status\n   - \"Run unit tests\" step failed\n   - \"Determine overall status\" step failed with `failed_step=Unit tests`\n   - `deploy-qa` job is **skipped** (not run)\n\n3. **Check Telegram:**\n   - Notification received with:\n     ```\n     🚨 CI Failure\n     Failed step: Unit tests\n     Logs: [link]\n     ```\n\n4. **Cleanup:**\n   ```bash\n   git rm tests/test_temporary.py\n   git commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test failure\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## AC-6: Success Path Unchanged\n\n**Given** all tests pass in CI  \n**When** the CI job completes  \n**Then**:\n- CI job status is **success** (green ✅)\n- `deploy-qa` job runs (triggered by `needs: ci`)\n- Telegram notifications for both CI success and deploy success\n\n**Verification (normal operation):**\n\n1. **Push valid change:**\n   ```bash\n   # Make trivial documentation change\n   echo \"# Test CI\" >> docs/test_ci.md\n   git add docs/test_ci.md\n   git commit -m \"Test: Verify CI passes and deploys\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n2. **Observe GitHub Actions:**\n   - CI job shows ✅ green status\n   - All steps passed (lint + tests)\n   - `deploy-qa` job runs after CI completes\n   - QA deployment succeeds\n\n3. **Check Telegram:**\n   - First notification:\n     ```\n     ✅ CI passed\n     Commit: [hash]\n     Message: Test: Verify CI passes and deploys\n     ```\n   - Second notification (after deploy):\n     ```\n     🚀 QA Deploy Success\n     URL: https://qa.fedes.dev\n     ```\n\n4. **Cleanup:**\n   ```bash\n   git rm docs/test_ci.md\n   git commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test file\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n### EC-1: Empty Test Suite\n**Given** no tests exist in `tests/` directory  \n**When** CI runs  \n**Then** pytest reports \"no tests collected\" but **exits 0** (success)\n\n**Expected behavior:** CI passes (no tests = no failures)\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Check pytest behavior with no tests\npytest --collect-only tests/ | grep \"no tests collected\"\necho $?  # Should be 0 (success)\n```\n\n### EC-2: Database Service Failure\n**Given** PostgreSQL service fails to start  \n**When** test step attempts to run  \n**Then**:\n- Tests fail with connection error\n- CI job fails\n- Deployment blocked\n\n**Expected behavior:** Health checks should prevent this (service has `--health-cmd pg_isready`)\n\n**Monitoring:** Check GitHub Actions logs for PostgreSQL service health\n\n### EC-3: Import Errors\n**Given** tests have import errors (e.g., missing dependency)  \n**When** pytest collects tests  \n**Then**:\n- Pytest reports collection error\n- CI job fails\n- Deployment blocked\n\n**Expected behavior:** Same as test failure (blocks deployment)\n\n### EC-4: Timeout (No Response)\n**Given** a test hangs indefinitely  \n**When** CI runs tests  \n**Then**:\n- GitHub Actions job timeout (default: 360 min, unlikely to hit)\n- Job fails\n- Deployment blocked\n\n**Expected behavior:** `maxfail=10` ensures fail-fast, but no explicit timeout on test step\n\n**Mitigation (if needed):** Add `timeout-minutes: 10` to test step\n\n---\n\n## Performance Criteria\n\n### P-1: CI Duration\n**Given** the full CI pipeline (lint + tests + deploy)  \n**When** all steps run successfully  \n**Then**:\n- CI job completes in < 10 minutes\n- Test step specifically < 5 minutes\n\n**Measurement:**\n- Check GitHub Actions duration in UI\n- Monitor over 10 runs to establish baseline\n\n**Acceptance threshold:**\n- 🟢 < 5 min: Excellent\n- 🟡 5-10 min: Acceptable\n- 🔴 > 10 min: Investigate optimization\n\n### P-2: Resource Usage\n**Given** tests run with PostgreSQL service  \n**When** monitoring GitHub Actions runner  \n**Then**:\n- Memory usage < 2 GB\n- No OOM errors\n\n**Expected:** Standard unit tests should be lightweight\n\n---\n\n## Negative Test Cases\n\n### NT-1: Lint Failure Still Blocks\n**Given** lint fails (ruff check finds errors)  \n**When** CI runs  \n**Then**:\n- CI fails before running tests\n- Tests are **not** run (fail-fast)\n- Deployment blocked\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Introduce lint error\necho \"import os,sys\" >> quantagent/temporary.py  # Multiple imports on one line\ngit add quantagent/temporary.py\ngit commit -m \"Test: Verify lint failure blocks\"\ngit push origin main\n\n# Expected:\n# - Lint step fails\n# - Test step doesn't run\n# - Deploy blocked\n```\n\n### NT-2: Test Step ID Correct\n**Given** test step is enabled  \n**When** examining step configuration  \n**Then** `id: tests` is present\n\n**Why it matters:** `steps.tests.outcome` is referenced in status determination\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\ngrep \"id: tests\" .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n# Expected: line containing \"id: tests\" (uncommented)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Integration with Existing Workflow\n\n### Telegram Notifications\n**Existing logic should work without modification:**\n\n1. **CI Failure Notification:**\n   ```bash\n   Failed step: ${{ steps.status.outputs.failed_step || 'Unknown' }}\n   ```\n   - If tests fail: `failed_step=Unit tests`\n   - If lint fails: `failed_step=Lint`\n\n2. **CI Success Notification:**\n   - Sent only if all steps pass\n   - Existing logic unchanged\n\n3. **Deploy Notifications:**\n   - Only triggered if `deploy-qa` job runs\n   - Blocked by CI failure\n\n**No changes needed to notification logic** — already handles test failures.\n\n---\n\n## Manual Test Procedure\n\n### Setup\n```bash\n# Clone repo and switch to feature branch\ngit clone <repo>\ncd QuantAgent\ngit checkout feature/QuantAgent-82t-ci-test-enablement\n```\n\n### Test 1: Verify Uncommenting\n```bash\n# Check file diff\ngit diff main .github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml\n\n# Should show:\n# - Removed: # (comment symbols) from lines 62-69\n# - Removed: continue-on-error: true\n# - Changed: maxfail=5 → maxfail=10\n```\n\n### Test 2: Simulate Success\n```bash\n# Push to main (after blockers resolved)\ngit push origin main\n\n# Monitor GitHub Actions:\n# 1. CI job runs\n# 2. Lint passes\n# 3. Tests run and pass\n# 4. Deploy job runs\n# 5. QA deployment succeeds\n\n# Check Telegram:\n# - ✅ CI passed\n# - 🚀 QA Deploy Success\n```\n\n### Test 3: Simulate Failure\n```bash\n# Create failing test\necho \"def test_fail(): assert False\" >> tests/test_ci_verification.py\ngit add tests/test_ci_verification.py\ngit commit -m \"CI Test: Verify failure blocks deployment\"\ngit push origin main\n\n# Monitor GitHub Actions:\n# 1. CI job runs\n# 2. Lint passes\n# 3. Tests run and FAIL\n# 4. Deploy job SKIPPED\n\n# Check Telegram:\n# - 🚨 CI Failure\n# - Failed step: Unit tests\n\n# Cleanup\ngit rm tests/test_ci_verification.py\ngit commit -m \"Cleanup: Remove test failure\"\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done (Testing Checklist)\n\n- [ ] AC-1: Test step uncommented in workflow file\n- [ ] AC-2: Correct pytest command (`maxfail=10`, markers)\n- [ ] AC-3: DATABASE_URL configured correctly\n- [ ] AC-4: No `continue-on-error: true` present\n- [ ] AC-5: Test failure blocks deployment (verified)\n- [ ] AC-6: Test success allows deployment (verified)\n- [ ] EC-1: Empty test suite handled gracefully\n- [ ] EC-2: Database service health checks working\n- [ ] P-1: CI completes in < 10 minutes\n- [ ] NT-1: Lint failure still blocks (not bypassed)\n- [ ] NT-2: Test step ID is `tests` (for status check)\n- [ ] Manual Test 2 (success path) completed\n- [ ] Manual Test 3 (failure path) completed\n- [ ] Telegram notifications received for all scenarios\n","numLines":435,"startLine":1,"totalLines":435}}}
