real concern is what happens in CI with PostgreSQL. The tests using SQLite with JSONB—like `test_position_monitor_constraints.py` and `test_r78_trade_pnl_calculation.py`—will likely fail in CI since they're trying to use JSONB features on SQLite. I should look more closely at how those test files are actually set up to confirm whether this is a blocker. But the conftest.py also has a `db_session` that uses SQLite (and it uses `Base.metadata.create_all` which would also try to create JSONB tables).\n\nBut wait - if main doesn't have JSONB in models.py, then on main these tests would work fine with SQLite. The issue is specific to the feature branch having JSONB in models.py.\n\nBut if these test issues are on this feature branch and not on main, they would definitely cause CI failures when this branch is merged!\n\nOK, so my assessment as tester:\n1. AC-1 through AC-4, NT-2: ALL PASS (verified by grep)\n2. Local test run: 66 passed, 10 errors (database not available locally = expected)\n3. CI risk: Tests using SQLite with JSONB would fail in CI even with PostgreSQL\n\nWhen I ran the full test suite locally, it immediately hit the failure limit on the first batch of tests that require DATABASE_URL. In the second run where I filtered differently, the JSONB errors surfaced. The key insight is that in CI, DATABASE_URL will be set so those initial tests pass, but test_position_monitor_constraints.py creates its own SQLite connection and would still fail with JSONB regardless. This is definitely a blocker for CI, though it appears to be a pre-existing issue unrelated to QuantAgent itself. The JSONB issue stems from tests creating SQLite databases locally when they should be using the PostgreSQL instance configured via DATABASE_URL in CI. The real problem is that `test_position_monitor_constraints.py` added a local SQLite fixture, which actually made things worse by overriding what might have been a PostgreSQL-aware conftest setup. I need to examine the conftest more carefully to understand what the original db_session fixture was doing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1238,"cache_read_input_tokens":53338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1238},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c01d0b6d-817c-43ca-ba9d-d72fdeeef887","uuid":"3f02a1e5-5f17-4716-8f3c-6ee817cde1c4"}
