{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01DDn2EzEWXSErtPFnMs4TMr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tester phase is complete. Here's the structured output envelope:\n\n---\n\n## Output Envelope — QuantAgent-82t — tester\n\n**Run ID:** `20260504T175326Z-QuantAgent-82t-tester`  \n**Result: PARTIAL**\n\n### Summary\n\nThe implementer's workflow change is **structurally correct** — all 5 static ACs pass. However, a **pre-existing JSONB/SQLite incompatibility** across 4 test files will cause CI failures even with PostgreSQL available, because those tests hardcode `sqlite:///:memory:` connections and cannot compile the JSONB column in `quantagent/models.py`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n| AC | Result |\n|----|--------|\n| AC-1: Test step uncommented | ✅ PASS |\n| AC-2: Correct pytest command (maxfail=10, markers) | ✅ PASS |\n| AC-3: DATABASE_URL configured correctly | ✅ PASS |\n| AC-4: No `continue-on-error` | ✅ PASS |\n| NT-2: `id: tests` present | ✅ PASS |\n\n### Test Run (CI command locally)\n\n```\npytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n→ 66 passed, 29 deselected, 10 errors (exit 1)\n```\n\nThe 10 errors are `test_backtest.py` (api marker) requiring `DATABASE_URL` — expected locally, **would pass in CI with PostgreSQL**.\n\n### Risk Identified: JSONB/SQLite in 4 Test Files\n\nTests in `test_portfolio_manager.py`, `test_position_monitor.py`, `test_position_monitor_constraints.py`, and `test_r78_trade_pnl_calculation.py` hardcode `create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")`. The models have `Column(JSONB)` — SQLite cannot compile this. These **will fail in CI regardless of PostgreSQL availability** (they don't use `DATABASE_URL`). This is pre-existing and not introduced by QuantAgent-82t.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-82t/20260504T175326Z-QuantAgent-82t-tester/run-report.md`\n- `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-82t/20260504T175326Z-QuantAgent-82t-tester/result.json`\n- `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-82t/20260504T175326Z-QuantAgent-82t-tester/quality-gates.log`\n- Commit: `15219971` on `feature/QuantAgent-82t-re-enable-unit-tests-in-ci-pipeline-main`\n- Beads comment: added to QuantAgent-82t\n\n### Next Step\n\nCreate a new issue to fix the SQLite/JSONB fixtures in the 4 affected test files before merging QuantAgent-82t to main. Quickest fix: mark those tests with the `integration` marker so the CI command (`-m \"not integration and not slow\"`) excludes them."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":75160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1074},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c01d0b6d-817c-43ca-ba9d-d72fdeeef887","uuid":"a742759b-f59e-4a5a-94ad-18ec5732ac66"}
